1
00:00:08,172 --> 00:00:11,833
Watch a candle burn, and the
answer comes before any thought.

2
00:00:11,913 --> 00:00:13,463
The flame is changing.

3
00:00:13,543 --> 00:00:16,484
Something is there, and
something is happening to it.

4
00:00:17,296 --> 00:00:19,924
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

5
00:00:20,004 --> 00:00:23,882
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

6
00:00:24,692 --> 00:00:28,321
Section 3 looked at one
question, mind and matter,

7
00:00:28,401 --> 00:00:31,505
and found the gap between them
made by the starting point.

8
00:00:31,585 --> 00:00:33,692
Underneath it was a default mode.

9
00:00:33,772 --> 00:00:36,396
Faced with what appears,
we ask what it is,

10
00:00:36,476 --> 00:00:39,960
really, and cannot rest
until a something is found.

11
00:00:40,776 --> 00:00:44,763
This section takes up the way of
reasoning that the default mode runs on.

12
00:00:44,843 --> 00:00:49,219
Not one question, but the logic that
decides which questions seem natural,

13
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:51,162
and which answers seem possible.

14
00:00:51,242 --> 00:00:53,431
I call it the logic of substance.

15
00:00:53,511 --> 00:00:56,420
Beside it, I set the logic of dependency.

16
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:02,500
The two use the same words. Change.
Cause. Identity. Continuity.

17
00:01:02,683 --> 00:01:03,689
The path.

18
00:01:03,769 --> 00:01:07,562
But they begin in different places, and
the same words lead them into different

19
00:01:07,642 --> 00:01:08,842
worlds.

20
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:11,180
First, the candle.

21
00:01:11,984 --> 00:01:17,330
Watch it for a minute. The flame leans,
steadies, shrinks when the door opens,

22
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:22,044
and recovers. Ask what is happening, and
the answer is there before any thought.

23
00:01:22,124 --> 00:01:23,761
The flame is changing.

24
00:01:24,564 --> 00:01:26,554
Notice the shape of that answer.

25
00:01:26,634 --> 00:01:29,420
There is a flame, and
something happens to it.

26
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:31,431
The flame is the stable one.

27
00:01:31,511 --> 00:01:33,972
The leaning and the
shrinking are what befall it.

28
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:38,320
If I ask what really changed, I go
looking for the one that stayed the same,

29
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,349
while its states came and went.

30
00:01:41,152 --> 00:01:44,632
Even after all the arguments
have been followed and accepted,

31
00:01:44,712 --> 00:01:47,951
this picture comes back the
moment attention is off duty.

32
00:01:48,031 --> 00:01:51,239
It is not a belief that a
counter argument can remove.

33
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:54,636
It is a pattern of inference,
working below argument.

34
00:01:54,716 --> 00:01:56,774
That is why I call it a logic.

35
00:01:57,572 --> 00:01:59,643
So, two starting points.

36
00:02:00,456 --> 00:02:02,781
The logic of substance starts with things,

37
00:02:02,861 --> 00:02:07,283
and then asks what happens to
them. Do they arise? Do they last?

38
00:02:07,363 --> 00:02:10,054
Do they move, end, stay the same?

39
00:02:10,134 --> 00:02:11,970
The things are taken as given.

40
00:02:12,050 --> 00:02:14,135
The questions are about their fate.

41
00:02:14,932 --> 00:02:18,240
The logic of dependency
starts one step earlier.

42
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,210
It does not begin with things.

43
00:02:20,290 --> 00:02:24,530
It asks how anything is identified
as a thing in the first place.

44
00:02:24,610 --> 00:02:29,680
And it finds that a thing is identified
only in dependence. On its parts.

45
00:02:29,760 --> 00:02:32,682
Its causes. What it is contrasted with.

46
00:02:32,762 --> 00:02:34,802
And the name under which it is picked out.

47
00:02:34,882 --> 00:02:38,461
No thing is found standing there
before that identification.

48
00:02:39,272 --> 00:02:42,335
So the two do not disagree
about the candle's fate.

49
00:02:42,415 --> 00:02:46,370
They disagree about whether there
is, before any identification,

50
00:02:46,450 --> 00:02:48,150
a candle whose fate it is.

51
00:02:48,230 --> 00:02:50,233
Everything else follows from that.

52
00:02:51,036 --> 00:02:56,287
Now, the word logic needs care, because
it is easy to hear in another sense.

53
00:02:57,088 --> 00:03:00,953
I do not mean that the Middle Way
has a special logic of its own.

54
00:03:01,033 --> 00:03:05,029
And I do not mean that emptiness
is reached by going beyond logic.

55
00:03:05,109 --> 00:03:07,637
I mean the necessity of a consequence.

56
00:03:07,717 --> 00:03:12,230
Whoever proposes something that exists
from its own side must say what it is.

57
00:03:12,310 --> 00:03:14,961
To say what it is, they must pick it out,

58
00:03:15,041 --> 00:03:17,067
by contrast and by name.

59
00:03:17,147 --> 00:03:19,920
And in picking it out, they
have made it dependent.

60
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,289
The proposal undermines itself.

61
00:03:23,084 --> 00:03:25,536
Three things follow, and they matter.

62
00:03:26,352 --> 00:03:27,784
It is not a survey.

63
00:03:27,865 --> 00:03:32,160
The logic does not look around the world
and report that no essences have turned up

64
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:37,626
so far. It shows what anyone proposing
an exception must already be doing.

65
00:03:38,428 --> 00:03:41,070
It ends in a negation without a thesis.

66
00:03:41,150 --> 00:03:46,178
It removes inherent existence, and
puts nothing in its place. Not a void.

67
00:03:46,258 --> 00:03:48,737
Not a ground. Not a better something.

68
00:03:49,544 --> 00:03:51,588
And it keeps the ordinary rules.

69
00:03:51,668 --> 00:03:54,142
It does not suspend non contradiction.

70
00:03:54,222 --> 00:03:56,275
It relies on it, throughout.

71
00:03:56,355 --> 00:04:00,555
The chariot cannot be both identical
with its parts and different from them.

72
00:04:00,635 --> 00:04:03,898
Fire cannot be both one with
its fuel and other than it.

73
00:04:03,978 --> 00:04:08,150
The analysis has its force because it
holds the other side to exactly these

74
00:04:08,230 --> 00:04:09,430
rules.

75
00:04:09,924 --> 00:04:14,151
I say this plainly, because it marks the
difference between the Middle Way and its

76
00:04:14,231 --> 00:04:18,979
imitations. A view that claims to
transcend logic can say anything,

77
00:04:19,059 --> 00:04:23,530
and so says nothing. The logic of
dependency says one thing exactly.

78
00:04:23,610 --> 00:04:27,312
What is proposed as standing on
its own is not found to do so.

79
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:30,639
What, then, of the famous refusals?

80
00:04:30,719 --> 00:04:32,990
Neither existent nor non existent.

81
00:04:33,070 --> 00:04:35,055
Neither arising nor ceasing.

82
00:04:35,135 --> 00:04:37,003
Are these not contradictions?

83
00:04:37,796 --> 00:04:41,081
They are neither. They
refuse a presupposition.

84
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:44,535
Ask: is the present King of France bald?

85
00:04:44,615 --> 00:04:46,913
There is no answer, yes or no.

86
00:04:46,993 --> 00:04:49,196
Not because the question is too deep.

87
00:04:49,276 --> 00:04:51,519
Not because logic has broken down.

88
00:04:51,599 --> 00:04:54,318
But because there is no
present King of France.

89
00:04:54,398 --> 00:04:58,018
The question fails, before
either answer could be true.

90
00:04:58,828 --> 00:05:01,116
Does the self exist, or not?

91
00:05:01,196 --> 00:05:03,657
Does this moment arise, or cease?

92
00:05:03,737 --> 00:05:05,410
These fail in the same way.

93
00:05:05,490 --> 00:05:08,983
Each one presupposes a bearer
with a status of its own.

94
00:05:09,063 --> 00:05:13,386
Something there, to exist or
not exist, to arise or cease.

95
00:05:13,465 --> 00:05:17,149
When no such bearer is found,
both answers fall together.

96
00:05:17,229 --> 00:05:21,402
The Buddha told Kaccāna that the
world mostly leans on two notions,

97
00:05:21,482 --> 00:05:24,038
it exists, and it does not exist.

98
00:05:24,118 --> 00:05:28,105
The one who sees arising and ceasing
as they are takes hold of neither.

99
00:05:28,904 --> 00:05:30,758
We have met this move before.

100
00:05:30,838 --> 00:05:35,350
In Section 2, the question of what a thing
is in itself fell away with the given.

101
00:05:35,430 --> 00:05:40,078
In Section 3, the hard problem fell
away with the fixed natures it needed.

102
00:05:40,158 --> 00:05:42,103
Logic was never suspended.

103
00:05:42,183 --> 00:05:44,295
The question had nothing to be about.

104
00:05:45,108 --> 00:05:48,062
Now go back to the candle,
and look for the carrier.

105
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:52,564
The flame at this moment is
wax vapour, air and light,

106
00:05:52,644 --> 00:05:56,005
that were not there a moment
ago, and will be gone the next.

107
00:05:56,085 --> 00:05:59,035
Nothing in the flame is the
flame across the minute.

108
00:05:59,115 --> 00:06:03,492
Take away the burning, and no flame
is left over, to have been burning.

109
00:06:03,572 --> 00:06:06,513
The noun is never found
apart from the verbs.

110
00:06:07,316 --> 00:06:10,488
But the verbs are not found
apart from the noun either.

111
00:06:10,568 --> 00:06:14,971
A flickering with nothing flickering is no
more available than a flame that does not

112
00:06:15,051 --> 00:06:19,306
flicker. The walker and the
walking, Nāgārjuna showed,

113
00:06:19,386 --> 00:06:22,431
are named together, and
neither is found first.

114
00:06:22,511 --> 00:06:25,383
The same holds for the
changer and the change.

115
00:06:26,184 --> 00:06:30,877
So the logic of dependency does not
replace the subject with a better subject.

116
00:06:30,957 --> 00:06:34,641
Not a process. Not a flow. Not an energy.

117
00:06:34,721 --> 00:06:36,339
That would be the habit again.

118
00:06:36,419 --> 00:06:38,934
A new passenger, in the old seat.

119
00:06:39,014 --> 00:06:42,467
It notices that the changer and
the change are named together,

120
00:06:42,547 --> 00:06:44,872
within a frame of before and after.

121
00:06:44,952 --> 00:06:48,042
And that the frame itself
does not stand on its own.

122
00:06:48,844 --> 00:06:52,450
What remains is change, met
without a thing that changes.

123
00:06:52,530 --> 00:06:54,543
The candle still burns down.

124
00:06:54,623 --> 00:06:57,369
The wax is shorter at
midnight than at dusk.

125
00:06:57,449 --> 00:07:00,711
You can say correctly when it
was lit, and when it went out.

126
00:07:00,791 --> 00:07:02,736
Nothing is lost from the burning.

127
00:07:02,816 --> 00:07:04,978
Only the passenger is let go.

128
00:07:05,058 --> 00:07:07,627
The something that was
supposed to ride underneath,

129
00:07:07,707 --> 00:07:10,362
staying the same while
everything about it differed.

130
00:07:11,168 --> 00:07:14,770
So these are not two worlds,
one false and one true,

131
00:07:14,850 --> 00:07:17,111
the second hidden behind the first.

132
00:07:17,191 --> 00:07:20,241
They are two ways of reasoning
about the same candle.

133
00:07:21,036 --> 00:07:23,596
The logic of substance is not stupid.

134
00:07:23,676 --> 00:07:28,270
It is how the habit reasons, and for
most practical purposes it is fast,

135
00:07:28,350 --> 00:07:32,156
and good enough. What it cannot
do is survive being looked at.

136
00:07:32,236 --> 00:07:35,444
The logic of dependency does
not throw away the candle,

137
00:07:35,524 --> 00:07:37,170
the burning, or the clock.

138
00:07:37,250 --> 00:07:41,427
It only stops supplying the one who was
supposed to be undergoing all of it.

139
00:07:42,232 --> 00:07:44,031
This can be tested at once.

140
00:07:44,111 --> 00:07:48,080
The next time the picture of something
changing comes, look for the something.

141
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:51,151
Not in an argument. In
what is in front of you.

142
00:07:51,231 --> 00:07:52,754
The sound that is fading.

143
00:07:52,834 --> 00:07:54,453
The thought that is passing.

144
00:07:54,533 --> 00:07:56,164
The flame that is leaning.

145
00:07:56,244 --> 00:07:59,267
Look for what is changing,
apart from the changing.

146
00:08:00,068 --> 00:08:02,465
The picture insists it must be there.

147
00:08:03,264 --> 00:08:07,197
This is Section 4, Part 1 of
the Dependent Arising series.

148
00:08:07,996 --> 00:08:11,358
The looking finds more
change, vivid and exact.

149
00:08:11,438 --> 00:08:13,305
And no changer behind it.

